A||||18||KillerX||How I do vertical doors like diablo? plz help||||12||
Z||000000||KillerX||10-29-2001||11:27 PM||||I’m from Strathroy, Ontario, Canada and my dad finally let me buy one of his fieros so iv been having fun with it (painting the interior etc.) but now I wanna do something wild yes i know people have told me doing vertical doors is probably impossible but i really wanna give it a try so if any1 has pics, info, web site anything! that helps me that would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Thank you guys again yer a great help!<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000001||fix||10-29-2001||11:59 PM||||First of all, welcome to the forum.  Secondly, those people who told you that vertical opening doors are nearly impossible to do are correct.  I hate to rain on your parade, but vertical doors on a fiero is a serious project that, to my knowledge, has yet to be done.  It would take more modifying than most people are willing to do.  You would need to cut and reshape the roof supports and even the area in front of, and to the back side of the door.  Just look at a fiero, and then look at a Lamborhini.  You will realize that there is more to vertical opening doors than you imagined.  With enough persistance and engineering know-how, it could probably be done, but I don't think I would want to do it myself.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||10-30-2001||02:43 AM||||this is how i would do it.  ]<P>the door would have to open outward before going up. so keep the original hinges but bolt them to a metal plate on the car side. then hinge the metal plat towards the top of the door to the car.  so now you have a door that will open regular and if you get under it you could push it up and it would rotate up towards the front of the car.  <P>since you only need the door to open about 2-3 inches before you can move it up    you could weld a little stoper to keep it from opening up all the way.    <P>now all you would need is a really strong gas shock or strut of some sort. maybe the kind used on minni vans or something. <P>so does that make sense?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sleeper||10-30-2001||03:06 AM||||this is how I would do it<BR>sell the fiero and save for a diablo||||reg||1
Z||000004||Elenor84||10-30-2001||03:34 AM||||GtMike....that makes perfect sence to me man....if I didn't have such a big project going on right now I would dive into this one...but seriously...keep me posted guys on any advances in getting these doors on a fiero...Keep up  the good work!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Elenor84||10-30-2001||03:53 AM||||Ok...sorry guys...I couldn't resist...I just drew up some possible machanic's of this and I think the pictures I drew might work...GtMike..tomorrow I'll draw good copies and send u an explination on how I did it.<BR>it includes welding a bit to the frame and cutting holes in the door frame...no big deal...maybe some more reanforcing welds to...other then that a hydro shock and 2 steel rods and sleaves and grease...I know this isn't making sence right now but wait tell I get the pictures...I think it could work...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
