Z||000008||TRiAD||10-30-2001||09:17 AM||||It's been done to a CRX, so I know it can be done to a Fiero. <P>He had the doors move horizontally about 3-4" first (no swing, just slid out like a drawer) THEN they rotated up. <P>You could do this, but it's serious modification (ie; expensive) and would make ingress and egress much more difficult. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||10-30-2001||09:34 AM||||You can get a screw-type door/hood mechanisim (similiar to what new minivans use to open the hatch & side door) at <A HREF="http://www.autoloc.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autoloc.com</A>   hope this helps a little.  Good luck.||||reg||1
